 7. 🧀 A grating problem 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Extreme heat is testing Italy's cheese banks, the vaults that hold Parmigiano Reggiano while it ages for years, Axios' Emily Peck reports .

 🐮 Zoom in: The particulars of dairy finance are perhaps as complex as the cheese itself.

 Producers don't want to wait years to turn a profit on sales while the cheese ages — anywhere from 1-3+ years. Farmers need regular income, so they hand over wheels of cheese as collateral for loans. Share this story . 

 
 
